From 224b3f9172311a7b08eca097b55115e56643886e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:21:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] LightSpMV: index arrays follow pastix_int_t

LightSpMV hard-coded int64_t row/column index arrays, but PaStiX passes its own
pastix_int_t arrays, so a PASTIX_INT64=OFF build fed 32-bit indices to 64-bit kernels
(wrong SpMV in GMRES refinement). Add lspmv_idx_t, 32-bit when PASTIX_INT64=OFF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
